Subject: [PATCH] A touch on a window that isn't RetroFE's goes to the extra screen too

The pedestal's touches carry a window ID that matches none of RetroFE's windows, so 0025's
fallback (for windowID 0) never ran and the touch bar stayed dead ("screen -1"). An unknown
window ID now takes the same path: pointer check, then the cabinet's extra screen.
---
diff --git a/RetroFE/Source/Control/PointerInput.cpp b/RetroFE/Source/Control/PointerInput.cpp
index f40d2bc..c82e93e 100644
--- a/RetroFE/Source/Control/PointerInput.cpp
+++ b/RetroFE/Source/Control/PointerInput.cpp
@@ -89,7 +89,9 @@ int PointerInput::screenOfWindow(Uint32 windowID) {
         SDL_Window* w = SDL::getWindow(s);
         if (w && SDL_GetWindowID(w) == windowID) return s;
     }
-    return -1;
+    // ArcadeMaster: a window ID that is none of ours (the pedestal's touch screen reports one) - treat it like no window
+    LOG_DEBUG("Pointer", "touch on window " << windowID << ", not one of ours");
+    return screenOfWindow(0);
 }
 
 void PointerInput::pulse(Gesture g, Uint32 now, int slot) {
